      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_sid">Detector: Windows domain SIDs</string>
      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_sid_Help">Enable or disable this detector.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: detectors.enabled.sid</string>
      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_infra_names">Detector: Infrastructure names (Kubernetes, Helm, ArgoCD, Compose …)</string>
      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_infra_names_Help">Enable or disable this detector.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: detectors.enabled.infra-names</string>
      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_tracking">Detector: Tracking in links (utm_*, click ids, Safe Links …) – removed</string>
      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_tracking_Help">Enable or disable this detector.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: detectors.enabled.tracking</string>
      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_custom">Detector: Custom terms</string>
      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_custom_Help">Enable or disable this detector.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: detectors.enabled.custom</string>
      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_learned_names">Detector: Names learned from e-mail addresses</string>
      <string id="P_detectors_enabled_learned_names_Help">Enable or disable this detector.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: detectors.enabled.learned-names</string>
      <string id="P_lists_custom_terms">Custom terms</string>
      <string id="P_lists_custom_terms_Help">Company names, project names, internal host names … One entry per line: term, or term|TYPE|replacement (e.g. Contoso|ORG|Firma). TYPE is e.g. ORG, PERSON, HOSTNAME, CUSTOM.

The entries are added to the user's own entries and are always active; the user can add further entries but cannot remove these.</string>
      <string id="P_lists_known_domains">Known domains</string>
      <string id="P_lists_known_domains_Help">Own domains that are always replaced consistently, also in host names (e.g. corp.local, contoso.com).

The entries are added to the user's own entries and are always active; the user can add further entries but cannot remove these.</string>
      <string id="P_lists_allow_terms">Allowed terms</string>
      <string id="P_lists_allow_terms_Help">Terms that are never replaced.

The entries are added to the user's own entries and are always active; the user can add further entries but cannot remove these.</string>
      <string id="P_lists_allow_domains">Allowed domains</string>
      <string id="P_lists_allow_domains_Help">Domains that are never replaced (public services, vendors).

The entries are added to the user's own entries and are always active; the user can add further entries but cannot remove these.</string>
      <string id="P_lists_allow_ip_ranges">Allowed IP ranges</string>
      <string id="P_lists_allow_ip_ranges_Help">Networks in CIDR notation that are never replaced (e.g. 8.8.8.0/24).

The entries are added to the user's own entries and are always active; the user can add further entries but cannot remove these.</string>
      <string id="P_llm_enabled">Enable LLM features</string>
      <string id="P_llm_enabled_Help">Screenshot → text and the result check via an OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.enabled</string>
      <string id="P_llm_base_url">LLM endpoint URL</string>
      <string id="P_llm_base_url_Help">OpenAI-compatible base URL, e.g. https://llm.corp.local/v1.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.base_url</string>
      <string id="P_llm_api_key">LLM API token</string>
      <string id="P_llm_api_key_Help">Bearer token for the endpoint. Note: policy values in the registry can be read by the users.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.api_key</string>
      <string id="P_llm_model">Text model</string>
      <string id="P_llm_model_Help">Model for the result check and the detector.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.model</string>
      <string id="P_llm_vision_model">Vision model</string>
      <string id="P_llm_vision_model_Help">Model for screenshot → text. Empty: text model.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.vision_model</string>
      <string id="P_llm_timeout">Request timeout (s)</string>
      <string id="P_llm_timeout_Help">Timeout for text requests in seconds.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.timeout</string>
      <string id="P_llm_vision_timeout">Timeout screenshot → text (s)</string>
      <string id="P_llm_vision_timeout_Help">Timeout for screenshot → text in seconds; vision models need much longer.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.vision_timeout</string>
      <string id="P_llm_verify_tls">Verify TLS certificate</string>
      <string id="P_llm_verify_tls_Help">Verify the endpoint's certificate.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.verify_tls</string>
      <string id="P_llm_ca_bundle">CA bundle</string>
      <string id="P_llm_ca_bundle_Help">Path of a PEM file with the CA certificates for the endpoint.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.ca_bundle</string>
      <string id="P_llm_verify_output">Result check</string>
      <string id="P_llm_verify_output_Help">Check processed text with the LLM for leftovers.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.verify_output</string>
      <string id="P_llm_verify_output_off">off</string>
      <string id="P_llm_verify_output_warn">warn about leftovers</string>
      <string id="P_llm_detect">LLM as detector</string>
      <string id="P_llm_detect_Help">Sends the ORIGINAL text to the endpoint. Only enable for an endpoint you control.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: llm.detect</string>
      <string id="P_ner_enabled">Enable NER plugin</string>
      <string id="P_ner_enabled_Help">Find names of people and companies with the local NER plugin (installed with the MSI feature NER).

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: ner.enabled</string>
      <string id="P_ner_helper_path">NER helper path</string>
      <string id="P_ner_helper_path_Help">Only needed if the helper is not in the program folder or its ner subfolder.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: ner.helper_path</string>
      <string id="P_ner_language">NER language</string>
      <string id="P_ner_language_Help">Language model(s) to use.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: ner.language</string>
      <string id="P_ner_language_auto">automatic</string>
      <string id="P_ner_language_de">German</string>
      <string id="P_ner_language_en">English</string>
      <string id="P_ner_language_both">both</string>
      <string id="P_image_faces">Detect faces</string>
      <string id="P_image_faces_Help">Detect faces in images (plugin, YuNet model, local).

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: image.faces</string>
      <string id="P_image_face_effect">Effect for faces</string>
      <string id="P_image_face_effect_Help">How detected faces are hidden.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: image.face_effect</string>
      <string id="P_image_face_effect_black">black</string>
      <string id="P_image_face_effect_mosaic">mosaic</string>
      <string id="P_image_face_effect_blur">blur</string>
      <string id="P_image_nudity">Detect nudity</string>
      <string id="P_image_nudity_Help">Detect exposed breasts, genitals and buttocks in images (plugin, NudeNet model, local).

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: image.nudity</string>
      <string id="P_image_nudity_effect">Effect for nudity</string>
      <string id="P_image_nudity_effect_Help">How detected nudity is hidden.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: image.nudity_effect</string>
      <string id="P_image_nudity_effect_black">black</string>
      <string id="P_image_nudity_effect_mosaic">mosaic</string>
      <string id="P_image_nudity_effect_blur">blur</string>
      <string id="P_image_text">Detect sensitive text in images</string>
      <string id="P_image_text_Help">OCR (plugin, local) plus the text detectors: IP, e-mail, secrets, custom terms …

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: image.text</string>
      <string id="P_image_text_effect">Effect for text</string>
      <string id="P_image_text_effect_Help">Only "black" is safe for text; pixelated or blurred text can often be reconstructed.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: image.text_effect</string>
      <string id="P_image_text_effect_black">black</string>
      <string id="P_image_text_effect_mosaic">mosaic</string>
      <string id="P_image_text_effect_blur">blur</string>
      <string id="P_image_codes">Detect QR codes and barcodes</string>
      <string id="P_image_codes_Help">Detect QR codes and barcodes in images.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: image.codes</string>
      <string id="P_image_code_effect">Effect for codes</string>
      <string id="P_image_code_effect_Help">How detected codes are hidden.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: image.code_effect</string>
      <string id="P_image_code_effect_black">black</string>
      <string id="P_image_code_effect_mosaic">mosaic</string>
      <string id="P_image_code_effect_blur">blur</string>
      <string id="P_image_watch">Offer image redaction for copied images</string>
      <string id="P_image_watch_Help">The clipboard watcher shows a popup "Redact image" when an image is copied.

If configured, the user cannot change this setting. Setting: image.watch</string>
